# ESO sidecar invariant

**Prerequisite:** `core.law-gate.mdc` (`AGENTS.md` Read this session). This rule is the authoritative statement
of the ESO sidecar invariant; it is not a mirror of an `AGENTS.md` section.

## The rule

```text
ESO = config + sidecar + observatory + control plane
ESO ≠ runtime
```

ESO **NEVER**:

```text
run
execute
chat
start / queue / claim / advance a run
spawn a host process
call a model
hold host credentials
```

Host **OWNS**:

```text
user prompt
conversation
execution
model selection
CLI / ACP / native agent
workspace
observation + evidence
```

## Forbidden terms in `eso/**`

```
flow_run · flow-runs · run-requests · claim · advance
worker_run · run_id · execution endpoint · chat endpoint
```

If activity must be shown, model it as **observation/evidence**, not as ESO run/execution.

Exception: `claim` in the sense of a documentation/evidence claim (e.g. `knowledge_edge_claim`) is not an
execution claim and is allowed.

## Check

`review` — any new route, table, type, UI control, or doc sentence that gives ESO a run/execution/chat concept ⇒
**reject**. The agent must move it to the host side or remove it.

